## Testing Standards

### Test Structure
```apex
@IsTest
static void testMethod_Scenario_Expected() {
    // Arrange
    // Act
    Test.startTest();
    // code
    Test.stopTest();
    // Assert
    Assert.areEqual(expected, actual, 'message');
}
```

### Good Tests
✅ Test behavior, use assertions, test edge cases, bulk data, descriptive names

❌ Constructor-only, no assertions, duplicates, trivial getters/setters

---

## Anti-Patterns (NEVER Do This)

### SOQL in Loops
```apex
// BAD
for (Account acc : accounts) {
    List<Contact> c = [SELECT Id FROM Contact WHERE AccountId = :acc.Id];
}

// GOOD
Set<Id> ids = new Set<Id>();
for (Account acc : accounts) ids.add(acc.Id);
List<Contact> c = [SELECT Id FROM Contact WHERE AccountId IN :ids];
```

### DML in Loops
```apex
// BAD
for (Account acc : accounts) update acc;

// GOOD
update accounts;
```

### Nested Loops
```apex
// BAD - O(n²)
for (Account acc : accounts) {
    for (Contact con : contacts) {
        if (con.AccountId == acc.Id) { }
    }
}

// GOOD - O(n)
Map<Id, List<Contact>> map = new Map<Id, List<Contact>>();
for (Contact con : contacts) {
    if (!map.containsKey(con.AccountId)) map.put(con.AccountId, new List<Contact>());
    map.get(con.AccountId).add(con);
}
for (Account acc : accounts) {
    List<Contact> related = map.get(acc.Id);
}
```

